      "notes": "Population PK-PD parameters, rabbit P. aeruginosa meningoencephalitis model\nS09 | DOI 10.1128/aac.02181-21 | Table 1 (Farrington et al. 2022)\nMale NZW rabbits 2.08-3.78 kg; 300 µL of 1 × 10^5 CFU/mL P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 injected intrathecally; meropenem 5, 10 and 30 mg/kg/dose q8h IV push (marginal ear vein) from 6 h after inoculation. Total duration of therapy not stated (Results refer to bacterial burden at 30 h after inoculation).\nSerial sacrifice at planned times; rabbits per dose group not stated (Results: \"A total of 51 rabbits\" including controls for meropenem).\nPlasma sampled at 0, 10, 15, 20, 30 min, 1, 2, 4 h (n = 36); CSF satellite rabbits at 10 min, 30 min, 1 h, 2 h (text n = 4 at 10 mg/kg and n = 8 at 30 mg/kg; Fig. 2B says n = 8). LC-MS/MS, LLOQ plasma 0.1 mg/L, CSF 0.01 mg/L.\nThree-compartment model (central, peripheral, CSF), Pmetrics. Clearance and volumes are per animal (L/h, L). Concentrations are in Fig. 2 only (not transcribed). Protein binding not reported.\nText: \"AUCCSF:AUCplasma of 14.3%\". \"an AUC:MIC of 42.57\" refers to the hollow-fiber model, not to rabbits.",
